    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d518">

                <pb facs="0807" n="786" sameAs="frus:frus1948v04/pg786"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">860D.00/8–548: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Smith</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret   urgent</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-08-05T20:00:00+03:00">August 5, 1948—8
                            p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1530. Though thus far refraining from directly attacking new Finnish
                        Government,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d518-f1"/> Moscow’s obvious displeasure
                    over Communists complete exclusion is shown by considerable space given Soviet
                    press last few days to highly critical comment by foreign Communist sources,
                    above all in Finland itself (for example mytels 1520 August 4, and 1523 August 5<anchor n="2" xml:id="d518-f2"
                    />). Apart from general considerations which may still call for policy of
                    “moderation” (see mytel 1282 July 9), Soviets
                    probably hope Fagerholm Government’s narrow basis of support will prevent it
                    from surviving long, and its eventual demise will consequently impair position
                    social democracy in that country.</p>
                <p>Sent Department 1530, repeated Helsinki 59.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Smith</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d518-f1" n="1" xml:id="d518-f1-content">
                <p>On July 29, 1948, Fagerholm had constituted a new Finnish Cabinet. All of the
                    Ministers except Enckell, who continued as Minister of Foreign Affairs, were
                    Social Democrats.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d518-f2" n="2" xml:id="d518-f2-content">
                <p>Neither printed.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
